Point 19 (Quantize / Snap Selection to Grid)\
\
   The editor could place notes on a snap grid and the BPM Sync tool could snap ALL BT/FX notes globally, but there was no way to quantize just a selected region, and nothing could quantize VOL lasers at all -- a real gap now that freehand laser drawing (v0.0.35/36) routinely produces off-grid anchor points. A Quantize tool in the Tools Hub (Edit) should snap notes and lasers in the active Select region (or the whole chart) to a chosen subdivision, with a partial-strength 'humanize' option, per-class targets, optional hold-end snapping, and a +/- one-step nudge.\
Status: SHIPPED in v0.0.43. Tools Hub -> Edit -> Quantize. Grid 1/4..1/48 (incl. triplets); Region = Current selection | Entire chart; Strength 0-100%; BT/FX/VOL target checkboxes; 'Snap hold ends too' toggle; live in-scope + off-grid count; +/- one-step Nudge. Core math is in chart.js (quantizeTickValue / quantizeRange / nudgeRange) as a single DOM-free source of truth -- laser quantize recomputes point ry against the snapped section anchor, keeps the first point at ry 0, and enforces monotonic non-negative ry; nudge shifts a section as a whole and clamps at 0. Unit-tested standalone (30 assertions, all pass). Undoable via Ctrl+Z.\
