   Now that the Quantize engine exists, the natural next step is non-uniform quantize: instead of snapping every object to an even grid, apply a groove template that offsets alternating subdivisions (e.g. 16th-note swing, shuffle, or a user-defined offset-per-step map). This would let chartists humanize or stylize timing while staying musically aligned, and reuses quantizeRange's range/target plumbing -- the only new piece is a per-step offset table feeding the snap target. A small set of built-in presets (straight, light/heavy swing, shuffle) plus an editable offset row would cover most needs. Read-only on data structure; fully undoable like Quantize.\
