Point 21 (Camera / Lane Event Round-Trip Persistence)\
\
   Camera & lane effect events (zoom_top, zoom_bottom, zoom_side, tilt, lane_toggle, center_split) were imported from KSH into chart.cameraEvents, were editable in the Camera Events panel, and drove the live preview camera -- but were silently dropped by BOTH exportKsh() and exportKson(). Exporting a KSH or saving/autosaving KSON discarded all camera work: a round-trip data-loss bug in an otherwise-complete subsystem.\
Status: SHIPPED in v0.0.44. (1) ksh.js exportKsh adds camera ticks to the per-measure line-spacing offsets set (odd 1/24-style ticks now land on the grid) and emits standard key=value camera lines (zoom_top=, tilt=, lane_toggle=, ...) immediately before the matching note line, so the importer -- which attaches pending events to the next note line -- resolves them to the exact tick. (2) kson.js exportKson writes a compact _cameraEvents custom field ([y,type,value] in raw editor ticks, matching the _sections/_glitchEvents convention; omitted when empty). (3) kson.js importKson parses _cameraEvents back with a type whitelist and defensive filtering. KSON pack inherits the fix (reuses exportKson/importKson). Tested with the real exports: 14 assertions covering KSH/KSON/pack round-trips, multi-event-per-tick, measure-boundary placement, empty-chart cleanliness, and malformed-input safety -- all pass.\
