Point 49 (v0.0.67 SHIPPED: Cover-Stack Legibility Guard -- a warning before Sudden+/Hidden+/LIFT blank the lane -- item (g))\
v0.0.67 ships item (g) LIFT + HIDDEN+ MUTUAL-EXCLUSION HINT, carried forward since Point 43. Sudden+ / Hidden+ (v0.0.42) and LIFT (v0.0.62) are each individually capped at 90%, but they STACK: chart.coverVisibleFraction(sud,hid,lift) = clamp(1 - sud - hid - lift, 0..1) can fall to near zero when two or three are dialled up together, leaving an unreadable near-blank reading strip with NO feedback -- and the v0.0.63 Cover->ms solver could itself push the stack there when it laid a solved cover on top of existing ones. Now a badge in the preview cover row reads 'warn NN% lane visible' whenever the stack leaves a cramped strip (amber 'tight', visible < 25%) or an effectively blank one (red 'blank', visible < 8%), so the chartist sees it before the lane becomes unreadable, and it clears itself the moment the visible lane returns above 25%.\
