v0.0.68 ships REACTION RANGE, a NEW system on the v0.0.56-67 green-number engine. The Green# readout (v0.0.56) only ever reported the reaction window AT THE PLAYHEAD, so on a soflan chart the reading-window swing between sections was invisible: a chartist could not tell that the fastest part demands, say, a 264 ms reaction while the rest sits at 912 ms, nor jump to that worst part. A new 'arrows Range' toggle in the preview Green# row scans EVERY tempo in the chart and shows 'arrows lo-hi ms' -- the fastest-reading (hardest) and slowest-reading (easiest) windows -- for the current HiSpeed, practice rate and Sudden+/Hidden+/LIFT cover; a wide swing (max/min >= 1.5x) paints amber. Clicking the readout seeks the editor to the hardest-reading (min-ms) section. In C-mode the constant scroll fixes the window across soflan, so a single dimmed value is shown instead of a range.\
