Point 56 (v0.0.74 SHIPPED: Peak Jack -- the honest single-finger stress number, the third physical-difficulty axis -- a NEW system) v0.0.74 adds PEAK JACK, a NEW system alongside the v0.0.56-70 green number (reading load: how long you have to READ a note) and the v0.0.71-73 NPS (whole-hand actuation: notes/sec both hands). Jack stress is the SAME-finger axis neither exposed: a jack is two or more notes in a row on ONE lane, so a finger must strike again and again -- an 8th stream shared across four BT lanes is a comfortable 8 NPS, but the identical 8 NPS all on BT-A is a punishing jack that reads identically to the density and reaction numbers. Verified first that yesterday's work (v0.0.71-73) is fully integrated and unbroken: chart.notesPerSecond / npsDifficultyBand / measureDensityNps / reactionWindowExtremes / reactionWindowProfile / profileSampleAt all present and correct via a 14-case node ESM smoke test (120bpm quarters -> 2 NPS; the SAME pattern at 240 -> exactly DOUBLE; measureDensityNps + computeChartStats fold-in); all 20 JS modules pass node --check; server.js serves index/app/chart (HTTP 200); a real-browser Playwright load switched with ZERO JS pageerrors (only the pre-existing offline /img/dev.jpg 404 and the unpkg CDN tunnel, neither a regression).\
