Point 57 (v0.0.75 SHIPPED: Hand Balance -- the honest left-vs-right workload number, the fourth physical-difficulty axis -- ships recommendation (ll) HAND-BALANCE / LR SPLIT NPS) v0.0.75 adds HAND BALANCE, the FOURTH physical-difficulty axis alongside the v0.0.56-70 green number (reading load), the v0.0.71-73 NPS (both-hands actuation) and the v0.0.74 jack (single-finger repeat). Hand balance answers a question none of those do: is the WORK split evenly between your two hands, or does one hand carry the chart? In SDVX the left hand plays BT-A, BT-B and FX-L; the right hand plays BT-C, BT-D and FX-R. A stream that reads as a comfortable 8 NPS overall can be a brutal one-arm run if every note lands on the left three lanes -- and no whole-chart NPS or jack number exposed that. Verified first that yesterday's work (v0.0.74 Peak Jack) is fully integrated and unbroken: a node ESM smoke test confirmed chart.jackStress / jackDifficultyBand present and correct and that computeChartStats folds the jack fields in matching a direct call; all 21 JS modules pass node --check; server.js serves index/app/chart (HTTP 200); a real-browser Playwright load reported ZERO JS pageerrors (only the pre-existing offline /img/dev.jpg 404 and the unpkg CDN tunnel). Per the 'come up with a NEW system, but if it already exists build on it' rule: confirmed absent -- grep for handBalance / lrSplit / leftHand / handedness returned nothing, and handsim.js is a 3D hand RENDERER, not a metric; this is recommendation (ll), listed NOT YET STARTED. Built it (v0.0.75): (1) chart.js gains handBalance(opts) -- a DOM-free source of truth that splits onsets into the left hand (BT-A, BT-B, FX-L) and right hand (BT-C, BT-D, FX-R), reuses the exact onset-anchored sliding-window sweep notesPerSecond uses to get each hand's PEAK NPS (so they agree with the whole-chart figure by construction), and returns leftPeakNps / rightPeakNps / leftTotal / rightTotal / leftPct / rightPct / heavier / heavierShare (0.5 = even .. 1.0 = one hand does everything); onsets only (a hold counts once at its start), lasers excluded as continuous knob motion, matching the NPS convention. (2) a new exported chart.handBalanceBand(share) classifies the lopsidedness Balanced (<55%) / Slight lean (55-65%) / One-hand heavy (>=65%) with a stable key + colour matching the difficulty-band palette. (3) computeChartStats folds the result in beside Peak Jack (guarded typeof chart.handBalance === 'function' so a plain-object caller degrades to even/zero, never throws). (4) A new 'Hand Balance (L / R)' row in BOTH the Chart Statistics modal (app.js) and the Tools-Hub Chart Statistics tool (tools.js) shows the L/R split %, the band label, the heavier hand, and each hand's peak NPS, driven by the shared band so the two can never disagree. Render-only -- the chart is never mutated; no KSON/data-format risk. Tested: 22 node ESM unit tests pass (empty -> even/0.5/zero, no throw; all-left -> heavier=left, 100/0, share 1.0, band strong, right peak 0; perfectly even 2+2 -> even/balanced; FX-L counts left and FX-R counts right; 60/40 -> lean; a 4-note 1/16 jack on BT-A -> left peak 4 NPS; computeChartStats fold-in exactly equals a direct handBalance call; a plain-object caller does NOT throw; every band boundary at 0.5/0.549/0.55/0.649/0.65/1.0 and NaN; no mutation). A real-browser Playwright run computed a deliberately left-heavy chart -> 88% / 13%, One-hand heavy, peak 7.0 / 1.0 NPS with ZERO JS pageerrors, and opened the Chart Statistics modal in the live UI to confirm the new row renders under Peak Jack in the Density block. APP_VERSION bumped to 0.0.75; CHANGELOG + docs Updates section + docs version badge updated; the STALE dated UPDATES log (which had skipped v0.0.72/73/74) was backfilled. Status: SHIPPED in v0.0.75. Recommendation (ll) is now SHIPPED. STILL-OPEN follow-ups carried forward (all render-only, no KSON risk): (a) PER-VIEW C-REF IN MULTI-CHART. (b) SOFLAN MARKER DENSITY FILTER. (c) GREEN-NUMBER AUTO-FOLLOW CLAMP INDICATOR. (d) COVER GREEN NUMBER IN MULTI-CHART. (h) LIFT PRESET BUTTONS. (j) COVER-TARGET HOLD. (k) COVER-TARGET IN THE MAIN GREEN ROW. (n) 'MAX COVER' ONE-TAP. (o) COVER-TARGET HOLD RE-CLAMP CUE. (q) CUE IN MULTI-CHART PANES. (s) FIT IN MULTI-CHART. (t) 'FIT' KEYBOARD SHORTCUT. (u) FIT TOAST/UNDO. (v) COVER-STACK AUTO-CAP. (w) GUARD IN MULTI-CHART PANES. (x) 'MAX-READABLE COVER' ONE-TAP. (y) REACTION-RANGE ON THE PLAY FIELD. (z) RANGE IN MULTI-CHART PANES. (bb) SEEK-TO-EASIEST. (ff) NPS ON THE PLAY FIELD. (gg remainder) PER-SECOND NPS STRIP in the preview. (hh) CURRENT-NPS READOUT. (jj remainder) USER-SET NPS TARGET. (kk) NPS BAND ON THE PREVIEW READOUT. (mm) NPS DELTA VS ANOTHER CHART. (nn) NPS-BANDED HEATMAP LEGEND. (oo) CLICK-TO-SEEK THE PEAK MEASURE. (pp) NPS HEATMAP IN MULTI-CHART. (qq) PEAK-JACK CLICK-TO-SEEK. (rr) LIVE JACK READOUT IN THE PREVIEW. (ss) PER-LANE JACK BARS. (tt) JACK ANOMALY UPGRADE. NEW recommendations building on v0.0.75's handBalance (all render-only, no KSON risk): (uu) LIVE HAND-BALANCE READOUT IN THE PREVIEW -- a compact L/R split bar in the preview Density row, banded, so lopsidedness reads live beside Peak NPS and the green number. (vv) HAND-BALANCE DELTA IN SPLIT VIEW -- show each pane's L/R split and the delta so two chart versions' handedness compare directly (the hand-balance twin of the proposed NPS-delta (mm)). (ww) PER-HAND JACK -- combine handBalance's hand grouping with jackStress so each hand's fastest jack is reported, distinguishing a one-hand jack-heavy chart from a one-hand stream-heavy one. Status: (a)-(d),(h),(j),(k),(n),(o),(q),(s)-(bb),(ff),(gg remainder),(hh),(jj remainder),(kk),(mm),(nn)-(pp),(qq)-(tt),(uu)-(ww) NOT YET STARTED. Orthographic Mode Overhaul (Points 2/6/16/18) remains the top open item.\
