Point 59 (v0.0.78 SHIPPED: Honest Level Estimate -- the six measured axes reduced to one SDVX level -- a NEW system) v0.0.78 adds the HONEST LEVEL ESTIMATE, the capstone of the measured-difficulty family (v0.0.71-77). Per the "come up with a NEW system, but if it already exists build on it" rule: confirmed absent -- grep for honestLevelEstimate / honestLevelBand / "estimatedLevel" returned nothing in js/, docs, or this log. The ONLY pre-existing difficulty estimate is drawDifficultyEstimate() buried in the Volatility density tool (tools.js), which is a VOLATILITY HEURISTIC (column-variance + raw note/VOL density with an S-curve), NOT a reading of the measured axes -- the same stylised-vs-measured split the Honest Radar drew in v0.0.77. Motivation: v0.0.71-76 grew six genuinely-measured axes and v0.0.77 drew them as a shape, but a chartist still had no single "what level did I just make?" number sourced from those honest axes. Implementation: a single DOM-free, unit-tested source of truth chart.honestLevelEstimate(raw) that REUSES chart.honestRadarProfile internally (so the level is literally a reduction of the radar polygon and the two can never disagree), takes the same raw object drawRadar already builds (readingMs/peakNps/meanNps/peakJps/heavierShare/peakKps), and returns { level, levelFloat, composite, peakScore, meanScore, peakAxis, driver, band, color, axes }. The blend is peak-weighted -- composite = 0.6*(hardest axis score) + 0.4*(mean of all six axis scores) on the shared 0..100 scale where ~100 = "Extreme for that axis" -- mapped linearly onto 1..20, because an SDVX level tracks the single hardest demand a chart makes with sustained breadth lifting it. So a chart Extreme on EVERY axis lands at 20, a one-dimensional gimmick (one axis maxed, the rest near 0) sits mid-scale (~14) rather than topping out, and an all-zero chart is 1 (the UI gates the display on totalNotes>0 so a note-less chart shows "--", not a false "level 1"). A shared chart.honestLevelBand(level) maps 1..20 into Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced/Expert/Extreme on the same calm-green -> hot-red ramp the radar spokes and stat rows use (neutral intensity words, NOT SDVX chart-slot names like NOV/EXH/MXM which are slots not level ranges). UI: a #cs-level line directly under the Honest Radar in the Chart Statistics modal (index.html + app.js drawRadar), showing "Est. level N Band -- driven by AXIS" in the band colour, with a hover tooltip that spells out the exact composite arithmetic; honestly labelled an estimate, not a verdict. Render-only -- the chart is never mutated; no KSON/data-format risk. Tested: 28 node ESM unit tests pass (empty -> level 1 Beginner no throw; every axis at its Extreme anchor -> level 20 Extreme; a JACK-only gimmick -> mid-high level with driver=JACK and strictly below all-extreme; half-anchors everywhere -> composite ~50 -> level ~10-11; monotonic in each axis; NaN/negative/undefined/string inputs all degrade to 0 not NaN; over-anchor inputs clamp at 20; all band boundaries 1/7/8/11/12/14/15/17/18/20 plus clamps and NaN). Two real-browser Playwright runs against the LIVE app chart (mutating app.chart then re-opening the modal): an empty chart shows #cs-level "--"; a 180-BPM 16th single-lane stamina chart read "Est. level 17 Expert -- driven by STAM" (composite 83.7 = 0.6*100 + 0.4*59 -> 16.9 -> 17), with ZERO JS pageerrors.\
